     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. A single 4,000 mg dose of ibuprofen is above the toxic range for a 70 kg adult (about 57 mg/kg), and 16,000 mg/day is five times the maximum daily dose. No indication calls for that, and it could cause serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Your confirmation doesn't change that, and you haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If it's a typo,** tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. Examples are 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg three times daily.\n- **If there's an unusual indication,** talk with your attending and a pharmacist. If they approve a non-standard dose, it will probably need to go through a pharmacy-verified override process, not routine order entry.\n- **If you need better analgesia or anti-inflammatory coverage,** I can enter a maximum-dose ibuprofen order (800 mg PO three times daily, 2,400 mg/day) or a multimodal regimen you choose."
      }
     ],
